# Playwright / browser login

UI verification on the live app uses the dedicated `cursor` user.

Credentials live in the **repo-root** `.env` (gitignored):

- `PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL`
- `PLAYWRIGHT_USERNAME` (`cursor`)
- `PLAYWRIGHT_EMAIL`
- `PLAYWRIGHT_PASSWORD`

Read that file when you need to log in. Do not ask the user for the password. Do not print the password in chat or commit it into rules.

Auto-review still classifies login/token MCP calls as credentials. `autoRun.allow_instructions` in repo-root `.cursor/permissions.json` only steers the classifier. To skip it entirely, add these tools to the MCP allowlist in Cursor Settings > Agents > Approvals & Execution (or `mcpAllowlist` in `permissions.json`): `Playwright:browser_fill_form`, `Playwright:browser_type`, `Playwright:browser_evaluate`. Allowlisted MCP tools run immediately.